As of XX/XX/XXXX, my Account balance showed {$14000.00} due. 

XXXX XXXX original amount was {$10000.00}. The current balance is {$9700.00} with 116 payments allegedly remaining, despite {$6700.00} having been paid to date. 

XXXX XXXX original amount was {$4900.00}. The current balance is {$5000.00} with 116 payments allegedly remaining, despite {$4100.00} having been paid to date. 

Discover alleges that I still have 116 payments remaining before the Loans will be paid off, in their estimation around the year XXXX. 

My current Account snapshot ( as of XX/XX/XXXX ) is attached as Exhibit I. 

It is clear there is something wrong with my Loans. The original disbursement amounts, alleged interest rates and changes, Discovers refusal to provide specific information, compared against my payments made to date ; none of it makes sense. The math does not calculate. Perhaps there was an issue in the servicing of my Loans. My balances should be much closer to zero ( although I can not calculate the exact amounts they should be, as Discover has refused to give me my interest rates applied for the payments Ive made, and the generic rate change table does not add up either ). This is predatory and punitive against student borrowers, a vulnerable class. 

With this Complaint, I am requesting that Discover Student Loans reduce my total Account balance to more accurately reflect the true Loan balances based on my payments made and the Loans terms, and provide me with a reduced payoff letter, as I have suffered thousands in financial damages having paid on these Loans whose balances have effectively never changed. 

Thank you, XXXX XXXX XXXX",,DISCOVER BANK,FL,33991,,Web,2024-04-04,Closed with explanation,Yes
