8700363,2024-04-04,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Under the guidelines of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, it is stipulated in 15 USC 1681 section 602 ( a ) that consumer reporting agencies must carry out their duties with fairness, impartiality, and respect for consumer privacy. Early Warning is recognized as consumer reporting agencies, and I, as the consumer, have the fundamental right to safeguard my private information, as reinforced by 15 USC 6801, which mandates financial institutions to uphold customer privacy and safeguard their nonpublic personal information. XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX and XXXX XXXX XXXX being financial institutions, falls under this mandate. As per 15 USC 1681 section 604 ( a ) ( 2 ), consumer reporting agencies can only furnish a consumer report with explicit written instructions from the consumer concerned. Neither XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX nor the consumer reporting agency Early Warning have my consent or written authorization to share this information. Any prior consent, whether verbal, non-verbal, written, or implied, is hereby revoked. Additionally, 15 USC 6802 ( b ) ( c ) requires financial institutions to inform consumers of their right to opt out of information disclosures to third parties. XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX and XXXX XXXX XXXX failed to inform me of this right, violating the law. Moreover, 15 USC 1681C ( a ) ( 5 ) prohibits consumer reporting agencies from including certain adverse information in consumer reports without proper authorization, which they have done without my permission. Furthermore, according to 15 U.S. Code 1681s2 ( A ) ( 1 ) and 15 U.S. Code 1681e, it is unlawful to furnish inaccurate information to consumer reporting agencies, and these agencies must maintain reasonable procedures to avoid violations. As per 12 CFR 1016.7, consumers have the right to opt out of reporting services at any time, and I am choosing to exercise that right and opt out of the reporting services provided by these agencies. Lastly, per the Privacy Act of 1974 ) the term record means any item, collection, or grouping of information about an individual that is maintained by an agency, including, but not limited to, his education, financial transactions, medical history, and criminal or employment history and that contains his name, or the identifying number, symbol, or other identifying particular assigned to the individual, such as a finger or voice print or a photograph ; this includes cosumer reports. No agency shall disclose any record which is contained in a system of records by any means of communication to any person, or to another agency, except pursuant to a written request by, or with the prior written consent of, the individual to whom the record pertains.",,"Early Warning Services, LLC",FL,33570,,Web,2024-04-04,Closed with explanation,Yes
