Since my daughter and I discovered EdFinancials mistake, we have each repeatedly contacted EdFinancials customer service team to resolve the issue. That month, I submitted formal inquiries through EdFinancials online portal informing them of their mistake in crediting my daughters account with payments that were clearly marked for my Parent loans. However, I received no indication that a correction had been made to my account. On XX/XX/XXXX, my daughter contacted EdFinancials customer support staff by phone, and was promised by EdFinancial that they would resolve the payment error on their end within 60 days. In a separate call with myself, my daughter, and EdFinancials customer support staff in XXXX, XXXX, EdFinancial again promised they would ( 1 ) fix the mistake with my Parent loans and my daughters Student loans with their financial department, and ( 2 ) not charge me for any interest accrued as a result of their mistake. Yet, in XXXX, XXXX, my daughter received an email from EdFinancial Services acknowledging the payment meant for my Parent loans, while failing to remove the {$45000.00} refund balance from my daughters Student loans. I have attached a copy of the email as Exhibit 5. In XXXX, XXXX, my daughter and I both received tax forms from EdFinancial that continue to show incorrect balances for each of our loans. I have attached a copy of the balance on my Parent loans as of XX/XX/XXXX as Exhibit 6.",,EdFinancial Services,TX,75098,,Web,2024-04-07,Closed with explanation,No
