My father and I continued to make payments as we always have, yet the issue continued to persist. As of XX/XX/XXXX, I had another past due balance of {$100.00}. I called at XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX and spoke with XXXX . Again, I explained the issue and immediately asked to speak to a supervisor. Instead of connecting me with a supervisor, she placed me on hold to research my claim. The call was disconnected because she did not return. I called back at XXXX and spoke to an agent who immediately connected me with, XXXX XXXX a supervisor. XXXX and I spoke for 40 minutes. XXXX and the agent prior to the transfer asked me if I made my payments online and I told both that I did make my payments online. XXXX said that if I make a payment online, I can pick what loans the payment is allocated to. He explained that the total amount we pay each month is split between 5 separate loans ( loan numbers : XXXX, XXXX, XXXX, XXXX, XXXX ). Each loan has an individual monthly due amount ( See attached photos for amounts ). He said that the loan number that is creating the error is XXXX, which has a regular monthly due of {$150.00}. He said for some reason the system does not allocate this payment fully, so it is only getting a portion of the payment, which creates the past due balance. He told me I could make a payment directly to that loan and it would prevent the past due amount. In the meantime, I went to look over the Pay by Loan section on their online XXXX. However, as I looked further into my loans, I noticed that the loan XXXX had a {$0.00} amount due and my next payment is not due until XX/XX/XXXX. I asked XXXX why this was and why is the regular monthly payment ( for that individual loan ) is still included in my overall monthly payment of {$600.00} if I am not paying it. He responded, I dont actually know. Let me look into it. He explained that all the times my father and I paid over our monthly amount due, it did something that would push the due date for this loan out further. 