ans nor is it being paid to my loan XXXX, which is my highest interest loan that will give the company even more money in the long run for the loan due to high interest. I asked XXXX again as to why the loans are not being allocated to all 5 loans and he said they are supposed to be allocated to the benefit of me ( the consumer ). I asked him how is it for my benefit when you are taking money, not applying it to the loan, and then charging me interest because the company delayed making my payments? Additionally, where did all of our overpayments go because we still owe a considerable amount of money for having paid $ XXXX {$400.00} over payment each month for 4 years. XXXX said that we have a large amount of overpayment, and this is what caused my due date for loan XXXX to be pushed out so far, but again, this goes against what the company posted on their website because one of my loans should be receiving an additional {$110.00} as I mentioned to XXXX. Furthermore, I said if one of my loans was receiving the additional {$110.00} ( say for instead loan XXXX, which is supposedly past due for {$100.00} ), then I would not have a past due balance. I told him {$110.00} is more than {$100.00}, so I would not owe a past due amount. He continued to say he did not know what is going on and that there must be something wrong with how the system is allocating the payments, but that I could make sure that didnt happen by paying an individual loan my {$200.00} payment. Since he and I were not able to resolve the issue, I informed him that I would be contacting a lawyer and the XXXX. ( However, after speaking with my father ( cosigner ), he advised to contact the Attorney General. ). He cancelled my pending payment to my overall balance and the call ended. 

